      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] In `lsm6dso_emul_set_interrupt_pin`, returning early on lines 73–77 when `active` is `true` and FIFO interrupts are disabled in `LSM6DSO_INT1_CTRL` leaves the GPIO pin in its previous state (so if the interrupt pin was already asserted before `LSM6DSO_INT1_CTRL` was cleared, a subsequent `emul_lsm6dso_set_fifo_count` call leaves the pin stuck asserted).\n\nComputing `int_enabled` and driving `!(active \u0026\u0026 int_enabled)` both ensures the active-low pin is deasserted whenever interrupts are disabled and eliminates the early-return branch:\n\n```c\nstatic void lsm6dso_emul_set_interrupt_pin(const struct emul *emul, bool active)\n{\n\tconst struct lsm6dso_emul_cfg *config \u003d emul-\u003ecfg;\n\tstruct lsm6dso_emul_data *data \u003d emul-\u003edata;\n\n\tif (config-\u003egpio_spec.port \u003d\u003d NULL) {\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\n\tbool int_enabled \u003d (data-\u003ereg[LSM6DSO_INT1_CTRL] \u0026\n\t\t\t    (LSM6DSO_INT_FIFO_TH | LSM6DSO_INT_FIFO_FULL |\n\t\t\t     LSM6DSO_INT_FIFO_OVR)) !\u003d 0;\n\n\tgpio_emul_input_set(config-\u003egpio_spec.port, config-\u003egpio_spec.pin,\n\t\t\t    !(active \u0026\u0026 int_enabled));\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/6004e2b7-5414-4dac-a398-e759d39999f4)",
